foreign  these small QR codes accompanied our  travel since the second year of the  coronavirus pandemic consisting of  intricate black and white squares  scanned by digital devices they are the  core of the digital covered certificate  launched by the European Union one year  ago helping citizens travel across  borders again  [Music]  globally more than 1.8 billion  certificates have been issued in digital  or paper format so far  67 countries have joined that system 27  EU member states three from the European  economic area and 37 Nations outside of  Europe  [Music]  the phase of the creation the World  Health Organization was one of the  partners who joined forces with Europe  to select the technical specifications  to register and validate once  vaccination status  soon the need for interoperable and  standard-based recording and recognition  of vaccination status against covid-19  for domestic and cross-border purposes  has been identified European covet  certificate initiative is responding to  that particular need  interoperability is a key function in  order to build a system connecting  dozens of countries to make this  possible the commission set up a digital  Gateway making National I.T systems and  allowing seamless verification of the QR  codes  the covert certificate came into effect  on July 1 2021 to enable free movement  within the EU during the pandemic the QR  code contains key information such as  name date of birth date of issue  vaccination and Recovery dates as well  as test records  the personal data remains on the  certificate and is not stored at any  level  the pandemic has definitely shown that  cross-border Access to Health Data is  key in the response to health  emergencies  the successful experience of the digital  code certificate created in only three  months has been the result of a joint  effort and a pragmatic approach  we managed to keep complexity at the  minimum that was difficult to fit  everything what was needed in this very  small QR code and at the same time to  ensure the security of the system and  the possibility to verify the contents  without using any online services for  that and that was made possible because  of a very smart way of packing that  information and encoding and digital  assigning it  in the coming few years the whole power  of digital Health tools will be  expressed by the European health data  space  the initiative presented by the European  Commission in May 2022 will support  National Health policies research and  the quality of healthcare thanks to the  cross-border exchange of Health Data  can really  enable us to address many challenges  together and these are all challenges  that we face when putting forward the EU  digital certificate and now that has  opened up further innovation in the EU  in the area of digital Health Solutions  similar to the digital covet certificate  may be implemented in other ways in the  future According to some health sector  experts QR codes could be used to check  information on other vaccinations or  even to share other data with health  professionals at the click of a button  foreign  [Music]

